    "Special Auditor (SA) and Special Research Student (SRS) – Hokkaido University\nSkip to content\nCheck out the\nFact Sheet\nto see the outline of student exchange programs.\nThe application for SA/SRS 2027 Spring is now open!\nFor Students from Universities with Inter-University Agreement\nStudents from universities with an\ninter-university agreement\ncan apply as Special Auditors or Special Research Students (SA/SRS) to study as exchange students.\n1. Special Auditor (SA)\nUndergraduates can apply to study as a Special Auditor (特別聴講学生) at Hokkaido University. Postgraduates who aim to take courses and acquire credits are also able to apply to study as a Special Auditor (特別聴講学生).\nStudents select one School/Graduate School of Hokkaido University to be enrolled in and take courses and earn credits. The field of study must correlate with their specialization at their home university.\n*Hokkaido University can provide “Specialized Subjects” to undergraduate students from their second year onward.\nTo find the most appropriate faculty, please refer to the website of each School/Graduate School from the following link.\nUndergraduate Schools\nAgriculture\nDental Medicine\nEconomics and Business\nEducation\nEngineering\nFisheries Sciences\nHumanities and Human Sciences\nLaw\n(in Japanese)\nMedicine\nPharmaceutical Sciences and Pharmacy\nScience\nVeterinary Medicine\nGraduate Schools\nAgriculture\nBiomedical Science and Engineering\nChemical Sciences and Engineering\nDental Medicine\nEconomics and Business\nEducation\nEngineering\nEnvironmental Science\nFisheries Sciences\nGlobal Food Resources\nHealth Sciences\nHumanities and Human Sciences\nInfectious Diseases\nInformation Science and Technology\nInternational Media, Communication, and Tourism Studies\nLaw\n(in Japanese)\nLife Science\nMedicine\nPublic Policy\nScience\nVeterinary Medicine\n2. Special Research Student (SRS)\nStudents whose main purpose of studying abroad is to do research rather than to take courses and earn credits, you can apply as a Special Research Student (特別研究学生).\nOverview\nProgram Details\nSpecial Auditor (SA)\nHalf-year or full-year exchange in which students are assigned to a particular faculty and take classes related to their specialized area, joining full-time students.\nSpecial Auditors are required to attend at least 7 classes/week (10 hours/week) from our school/graduate school per term.\nSpecial Research Student (SRS)\nHalf-year or full-year exchange in which students are assigned to a particular graduate school and undertake supervision and advice on their research, joining a research room or lab, same as regular full-time students. Please note that Special Research Students are not eligible to take courses.\nProgram Duration:\nSpring (One year): April 1, 2027 – March 31, 2028\nSpring (Half year): April 1, 2027 – September 30, 2027\nNumber of Students Accepted:\nBased on MoU, decided on a yearly basis. There will be a screening at each School/Graduate School. Not all applicants will be accepted.\nApplication Form:\nSent on a nomination basis\nScholarship:\nNot Applicable\nAccommodation:\nUniversity dormitory. Room assignment is decided by Hokkaido University.\nEligibility\nEligibility Requirements\n1.Special Auditor (SA)\nUndergraduates\nExchange students have a high academic record at their home university in the field of desired faculty.\nEquivalent to JLPT level N2 or higher (preferably native level)\nExchange students are required to be enrolled at their home university as a full-time student during the entire period of exchange.\nPostgraduates\nHigh academic record at home university in the desired field of the faculty\nEquivalent to JLPT level N2 or higher (preferably native level)\nSome graduate schools provide courses in English. You are required certain level of fluency in English if you take English courses.\nEnrollment at home university\nExchange students are required to be enrolled at their home university as a full-time student during the entire period of exchange.\n2. Special Research Student (SRS)\nHigh academic record at home university in the field of desired graduate school\nEnglish or Japanese fluency to communicate with academic supervisor.*\n*May vary depending on the faculty/supervisor.\nRequired Documents\nApplication form\nCertificate of Enrollment from the home university\n*Issued by the president or dean at the home university\nRecommendation letter\n*Issued by the president, dean (or supervisor) at the home university\nTranscript of academic record\n*For Postgraduates, both Undergraduate and Postgraduate academic records are required.\nPhotocopy of Certificate of JLPT\nPhotocopy of passport\nDigital Photo data\nTB Clearance Certificate (If applicable)\n*This is general information, and the required documents may vary depending on the faculty.\nImportant notice:\nAs of June 23, 2025, submission of a TB Clearance Certificate (Japan Pre-Entry Tuberculosis Screening *JPETS) became mandatory when applying for a Certificate of Eligibility (CoE) to the Philippines and Nepal.\nTB screening will apply to nationals of the Philippines, Viet Nam, Indonesia, Nepal, Myanmar, and China who intend to enter and stay in Japan as “mid- to long-term residents.\n*Regarding Indonesia, Myanmar, and China, procedures are being coordinated, and the commencing date is yet to be determined.\nThe applicable students need to submit the certificate through the international office or exchange coordinator to exchange-programs[at]oia.hokudai.ac.jp by email at least a month before the result notification.\n*At the time of application for CoE, the validity period (90 to 180 days) of TB Clearance Certificate must be within its validity period. Please confirm the issuance schedule, etc., with the designated panel clinics in advance.\nFor further information, please visit the website of Ministry of Health, Labour and Welfare of Japan.\nYou can see the designated panel clinics and their process.\nJapan Pre-Entry Tuberculosis Screening / Ministry of Health, Labour and Welfare of Japan\nApplying\nHow to Apply\nPre-admission Support System (PSS) for SRS is now open!\n(Before applying) Students must obtain provisional approval from their prospective supervisor via PSS. (*Only for SRS)\nWe send application information and nomination sheet to the international office or exchange coordinator of our partner universities twice a year, in late August for Spring semester and mid-December for Fall semester.\nFill in the sheet by the international office or exchange coordinator of our partner universities and send it back to exchange-programs[at]oia.hokudai.ac.jp.\nWe send the document for Certificate of Eligibility, and the link to access the application forms will be individually sent only to the international office or exchange coordinator of our partner universities with nominees.\nApplicants and the international office or exchange coordinator submit the application documents on TAO (The Admissions Office) system and submit the document for Certificate of Eligibility to exchange-programs[at]oia.hokudai.ac.jp by email by the deadline.\n*The applicants for SRS at the applicable faculties must obtain a provisional approval from their prospective supervisor by using the Pre-admission Support System (PSS) before applying. The code with provisional approval (PSS code) is required for the application.\nHokkaido University screens the application.\nHokkaido University notifies the screening results to the international office or exchange coordinator of our partner university and gives further instructions.\nWe do not accept nominations and applications from individual students. Please apply through the division in charge of exchange mobility.\nDetails for the application\ndiffer for\neach School/Graduate School, so please follow the directions of each faculty to complete the application. Policy for course registration, including restrictions or limitations, might differ for\neach School/Graduate School.\nPlease follow the guidelines of each School/Graduate School for the detailed application guidelines.\nImportant Dates\nNomination Deadline:\n[Spring Semester 2027] September 25, 2026\nApplication Deadline:\n[Spring Semester 2027] November 13, 2026\nResult Notification:\n[Spring Semester 2027] Early February, 2027\nNote (SA Postgraduates/SRS)\n:\nChina Scholarship Council (CSC) *Chinese Universities Only*\nCSC applicants must be nominated at least one month before the deadline above if they need provisional acceptance earlier.\nIf you have CSC applicants,\nplease contact us earlier.\nCSC Joint Doctoral Program Researchers who aim to receive supervision on the research work are accepted as SRS at Hokkaido University. They need to be nominated and go through application procedures as SRS applicants. If a student individually contacts a professor and is promised acceptance, the procedures will be ineffective or incomplete. Please go through the proper application procedures through the home university exchange office and the Student Exchange Division of Hokkaido University.\nFrequently Asked Questions\nPlease see\nQ&A\nbefore asking questions.\nUpdated on\nAugust 20, 2026\nShare\nFacebook\nX\nLinkedin\nBluesky\nThreads"
  ],
